{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your page already has WebMCP tools. A widget, a library, or your own code registered them on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"document.modelContext"},{"type":"text","value":". You want your in-page chat to use the same tools, without a second copy of each tool."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The page tools API reads the tools from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"document.modelContext"},{"type":"text","value":" and gives them to the chat as client tools. When the model calls a tool, the chat runs the tool through WebMCP."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Experimental:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" WebMCP support is experimental. During SSR, in insecure contexts, or in unsupported browsers, the tool list stays empty."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-accept-client-tools-on-the-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Accept client tools on the server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server does not know the page tools. Let the client declare them with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mergeAgentTools"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// api/chat.ts\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  mergeAgentTools,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-6-astra'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    tools: mergeAgentTools([], params.tools),\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Security:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params.tools"},{"type":"text","value":" comes from the browser. The model can call these tools, but the tools run in the browser, not on the server. Keep sensitive work behind your own server checks."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-give-the-page-tools-to-the-chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Give the page tools to the chat"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the page tools API for your framework. Pass the result to the chat as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usePageWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" returns an array. The array updates when the page adds or removes a tool."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({ connection, tools: pageTools })\n\n  return (\n    <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n      Ask ({messages.length} messages)\n    </button>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"vue"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usePageWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" returns a ref. Pass the ref to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-vue'\n\nconst pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\nconst { sendMessage } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: pageTools,\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <button type=\"button\" @click=\"sendMessage('Open the help panel')\">\n    Ask\n  </button>\n</template>","lang":"vue"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usePageWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" returns an accessor. Read it in a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" getter."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    get tools() {\n      return pageTools()\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n      Ask\n    </button>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"svelte"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createPageWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" returns an object with a reactive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" field. Read it in a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" getter."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import {\n    createChat,\n    createPageWebMCPTools,\n    fetchServerSentEvents,\n  } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n\n  const page = createPageWebMCPTools()\n  const chat = createChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    get tools() {\n      return page.tools\n    },\n  })\n</script>\n\n<button type=\"button\" onclick={() => chat.sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n  Ask\n</button>","lang":"svelte"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"preact"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usePageWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" returns an array. The array updates when the page adds or removes a tool."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-preact'\n\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({ connection, tools: pageTools })\n\n  return (\n    <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n      Ask\n    </button>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"angular"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectPageWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" returns a signal. Pass the signal to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectChat"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  injectChat,\n  injectPageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-angular'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-chat',\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `<button type=\"button\" (click)=\"ask()\">Ask</button>`,\n})\nexport class Chat {\n  pageTools = injectPageWebMCPTools()\n  chat = injectChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    tools: this.pageTools,\n  })\n\n  ask() {\n    void this.chat.sendMessage('Open the help panel')\n  }\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"octane"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usePageWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" returns an array. The array updates when the page adds or removes a tool."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-octane'\n\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({ connection, tools: pageTools })\n\n  return (\n    <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n      Ask\n    </button>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"remix"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the component "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Handle"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createPageWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":". It calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handle.update()"},{"type":"text","value":" when the tools change. Read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"page.tools"},{"type":"text","value":" in a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" getter. The chat reads the getter each time a run starts."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createChat,\n  createPageWebMCPTools,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-remix'\nimport { clientEntry, createElement, on } from 'remix/ui'\n\nexport const Chat = clientEntry(import.meta.url, function Chat(handle) {\n  const page = createPageWebMCPTools(handle)\n  const chat = createChat(handle, {\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    get tools() {\n      return page.tools\n    },\n  })\n\n  return () =>\n    createElement(\n      'button',\n      {\n        type: 'button',\n        mix: on<HTMLButtonElement>('click', () => {\n          void chat.sendMessage('Open the help panel')\n        }),\n      },\n      'Ask',\n    )\n})","lang":"tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"vue\",\"solid\",\"svelte\",\"preact\",\"angular\",\"octane\",\"remix\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\\n  useChat,\\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\\n\\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\\n\\nexport function Chat() {\\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({ connection, tools: pageTools })\\n\\n  return (\\n    <button type=\\\"button\\\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\\n      Ask ({messages.length} messages)\\n    </button>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"vue\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"<script setup lang=\\\"ts\\\">\\nimport {\\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\\n  useChat,\\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\\n} from '@tanstack/ai-vue'\\n\\nconst pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\\nconst { sendMessage } = useChat({\\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\\n  tools: pageTools,\\n})\\n</script>\\n\\n<template>\\n  <button type=\\\"button\\\" @click=\\\"sendMessage('Open the help panel')\\\">\\n    Ask\\n  </button>\\n</template>\",\"language\":\"vue\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\\n  useChat,\\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\\n} from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\\n\\nexport function Chat() {\\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({\\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\\n    get tools() {\\n      return pageTools()\\n    },\\n  })\\n\\n  return (\\n    <button type=\\\"button\\\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\\n      Ask\\n    </button>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"svelte\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"<script lang=\\\"ts\\\">\\n  import {\\n    createChat,\\n    createPageWebMCPTools,\\n    fetchServerSentEvents,\\n  } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\\n\\n  const page = createPageWebMCPTools()\\n  const chat = createChat({\\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\\n    get tools() {\\n      return page.tools\\n    },\\n  })\\n</script>\\n\\n<button type=\\\"button\\\" onclick={() => chat.sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\\n  Ask\\n</button>\",\"language\":\"svelte\"}],\"preact\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\\n  useChat,\\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\\n} from '@tanstack/ai-preact'\\n\\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\\n\\nexport function Chat() {\\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({ connection, tools: pageTools })\\n\\n  return (\\n    <button type=\\\"button\\\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\\n      Ask\\n    </button>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"angular\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { Component } from '@angular/core'\\nimport {\\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\\n  injectChat,\\n  injectPageWebMCPTools,\\n} from '@tanstack/ai-angular'\\n\\n@Component({\\n  selector: 'app-chat',\\n  standalone: true,\\n  template: `<button type=\\\"button\\\" (click)=\\\"ask()\\\">Ask</button>`,\\n})\\nexport class Chat {\\n  pageTools = injectPageWebMCPTools()\\n  chat = injectChat({\\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\\n    tools: this.pageTools,\\n  })\\n\\n  ask() {\\n    void this.chat.sendMessage('Open the help panel')\\n  }\\n}\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"octane\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\\n  useChat,\\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\\n} from '@tanstack/ai-octane'\\n\\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\\n\\nexport function Chat() {\\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({ connection, tools: pageTools })\\n\\n  return (\\n    <button type=\\\"button\\\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\\n      Ask\\n    </button>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"remix\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  createChat,\\n  createPageWebMCPTools,\\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\\n} from '@tanstack/ai-remix'\\nimport { clientEntry, createElement, on } from 'remix/ui'\\n\\nexport const Chat = clientEntry(import.meta.url, function Chat(handle) {\\n  const page = createPageWebMCPTools(handle)\\n  const chat = createChat(handle, {\\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\\n    get tools() {\\n      return page.tools\\n    },\\n  })\\n\\n  return () =>\\n    createElement(\\n      'button',\\n      {\\n        type: 'button',\\n        mix: on<HTMLButtonElement>('click', () => {\\n          void chat.sendMessage('Open the help panel')\\n        }),\\n      },\\n      'Ask',\\n    )\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-skip-tools-with-a-filter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Skip tools with a filter"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filter"},{"type":"text","value":" to skip a tool. Return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" and the chat does not get that tool. The filter gets the WebMCP tool, so you can read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"annotations"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { usePageWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nexport function useReadOnlyPageTools() {\n  return usePageWebMCPTools({\n    filter: (tool) =>\n      tool.origin === location.origin &&\n      tool.annotations?.readOnlyHint === true,\n  })\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every framework API takes the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filter"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":" options. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":" gets a failed WebMCP read, for example a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotAllowedError"},{"type":"text","value":" from the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" permissions policy. The last good list stays in place."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool names must be unique after filtering, including tools from different frames. If names repeat, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getWebMCPTools()"},{"type":"text","value":" rejects and subscriptions report the error through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":". Subscriptions keep the last good list. Give the tools unique names or use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filter"},{"type":"text","value":" to select one of them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some providers reject a tool name with a period, such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"help.open"},{"type":"text","value":". WebMCP allows periods. Skip those tools with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filter"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"read-page-tools-without-a-framework","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read page tools without a framework"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-client"},{"type":"text","value":" to read the tools one time:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { ChatClient, fetchServerSentEvents, getWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: await getWebMCPTools(),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To keep the list current, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subscribeWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":". It calls your listener now and after each WebMCP "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolchange"},{"type":"text","value":" event. Abort the signal to stop:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  ChatClient,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  subscribeWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-client'\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n})\nconst subscription = new AbortController()\n\nsubscribeWebMCPTools((tools) => client.updateOptions({ tools }), {\n  signal: subscription.signal,\n  filter: (tool) => tool.origin === location.origin,\n})\n\nexport function stopPageTools() {\n  subscription.abort()\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every framework package also exports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subscribeWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your chat can now call every WebMCP tool on the page that passes your filter. To expose your own client tools to WebMCP, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./webmcp","children":[{"type":"text","value":"WebMCP Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-accept-client-tools-on-the-server","text":"1. Accept client tools on the server","level":2},{"id":"2-give-the-page-tools-to-the-chat","text":"2. Give the page tools to the chat","level":2},{"id":"3-skip-tools-with-a-filter","text":"3. Skip tools with a filter","level":2},{"id":"read-page-tools-without-a-framework","text":"Read page tools without a framework","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","octane","remix"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYour page already has WebMCP tools. A widget, a library, or your own code registered them on `document.modelContext`. You want your in-page chat to use the same tools, without a second copy of each tool.\n\nThe page tools API reads the tools from `document.modelContext` and gives them to the chat as client tools. When the model calls a tool, the chat runs the tool through WebMCP.\n\n> **Experimental:** WebMCP support is experimental. During SSR, in insecure contexts, or in unsupported browsers, the tool list stays empty.\n\n## 1. Accept client tools on the server\n\nThe server does not know the page tools. Let the client declare them with `mergeAgentTools`:\n\n```ts\n// api/chat.ts\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  mergeAgentTools,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-6-astra'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    tools: mergeAgentTools([], params.tools),\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\n> **Security:** `params.tools` comes from the browser. The model can call these tools, but the tools run in the browser, not on the server. Keep sensitive work behind your own server checks.\n\n## 2. Give the page tools to the chat\n\nUse the page tools API for your framework. Pass the result to the chat as `tools`.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n`usePageWebMCPTools` returns an array. The array updates when the page adds or removes a tool.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({ connection, tools: pageTools })\n\n  return (\n    <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n      Ask ({messages.length} messages)\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Vue\n\n`usePageWebMCPTools` returns a ref. Pass the ref to `useChat`.\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-vue'\n\nconst pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\nconst { sendMessage } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: pageTools,\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <button type=\"button\" @click=\"sendMessage('Open the help panel')\">\n    Ask\n  </button>\n</template>\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n`usePageWebMCPTools` returns an accessor. Read it in a `tools` getter.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    get tools() {\n      return pageTools()\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n      Ask\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Svelte\n\n`createPageWebMCPTools` returns an object with a reactive `tools` field. Read it in a `tools` getter.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import {\n    createChat,\n    createPageWebMCPTools,\n    fetchServerSentEvents,\n  } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n\n  const page = createPageWebMCPTools()\n  const chat = createChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    get tools() {\n      return page.tools\n    },\n  })\n</script>\n\n<button type=\"button\" onclick={() => chat.sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n  Ask\n</button>\n```\n\n# Preact\n\n`usePageWebMCPTools` returns an array. The array updates when the page adds or removes a tool.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-preact'\n\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({ connection, tools: pageTools })\n\n  return (\n    <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n      Ask\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Angular\n\n`injectPageWebMCPTools` returns a signal. Pass the signal to `injectChat`.\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  injectChat,\n  injectPageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-angular'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-chat',\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `<button type=\"button\" (click)=\"ask()\">Ask</button>`,\n})\nexport class Chat {\n  pageTools = injectPageWebMCPTools()\n  chat = injectChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    tools: this.pageTools,\n  })\n\n  ask() {\n    void this.chat.sendMessage('Open the help panel')\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Octane\n\n`usePageWebMCPTools` returns an array. The array updates when the page adds or removes a tool.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-octane'\n\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({ connection, tools: pageTools })\n\n  return (\n    <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n      Ask\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Remix\n\nPass the component `Handle` to `createPageWebMCPTools`. It calls `handle.update()` when the tools change. Read `page.tools` in a `tools` getter. The chat reads the getter each time a run starts.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createChat,\n  createPageWebMCPTools,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-remix'\nimport { clientEntry, createElement, on } from 'remix/ui'\n\nexport const Chat = clientEntry(import.meta.url, function Chat(handle) {\n  const page = createPageWebMCPTools(handle)\n  const chat = createChat(handle, {\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    get tools() {\n      return page.tools\n    },\n  })\n\n  return () =>\n    createElement(\n      'button',\n      {\n        type: 'button',\n        mix: on<HTMLButtonElement>('click', () => {\n          void chat.sendMessage('Open the help panel')\n        }),\n      },\n      'Ask',\n    )\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## 3. Skip tools with a filter\n\nPass `filter` to skip a tool. Return `false` and the chat does not get that tool. The filter gets the WebMCP tool, so you can read `name`, `origin`, and `annotations`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { usePageWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nexport function useReadOnlyPageTools() {\n  return usePageWebMCPTools({\n    filter: (tool) =>\n      tool.origin === location.origin &&\n      tool.annotations?.readOnlyHint === true,\n  })\n}\n```\n\nEvery framework API takes the same `filter` and `onError` options. `onError` gets a failed WebMCP read, for example a `NotAllowedError` from the `tools` permissions policy. The last good list stays in place.\n\nTool names must be unique after filtering, including tools from different frames. If names repeat, `getWebMCPTools()` rejects and subscriptions report the error through `onError`. Subscriptions keep the last good list. Give the tools unique names or use `filter` to select one of them.\n\nSome providers reject a tool name with a period, such as `help.open`. WebMCP allows periods. Skip those tools with `filter`.\n\n## Read page tools without a framework\n\nUse `getWebMCPTools` from `@tanstack/ai-client` to read the tools one time:\n\n```ts\nimport { ChatClient, fetchServerSentEvents, getWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: await getWebMCPTools(),\n})\n```\n\nTo keep the list current, use `subscribeWebMCPTools`. It calls your listener now and after each WebMCP `toolchange` event. Abort the signal to stop:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  ChatClient,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  subscribeWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-client'\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n})\nconst subscription = new AbortController()\n\nsubscribeWebMCPTools((tools) => client.updateOptions({ tools }), {\n  signal: subscription.signal,\n  filter: (tool) => tool.origin === location.origin,\n})\n\nexport function stopPageTools() {\n  subscription.abort()\n}\n```\n\nEvery framework package also exports `getWebMCPTools` and `subscribeWebMCPTools`.\n\nYour chat can now call every WebMCP tool on the page that passes your filter. To expose your own client tools to WebMCP, see [WebMCP Tools](./webmcp).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Page WebMCP Tools in Chat\nid: webmcp-page-tools\norder: 6\ndescription: \"Read the WebMCP tools that a page registers and give them to your TanStack AI chat as client tools.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - webmcp\n  - browser tools\n  - client tools\n  - usePageWebMCPTools\n  - createPageWebMCPTools\n  - injectPageWebMCPTools\n  - getWebMCPTools\n---\n\nYour page already has WebMCP tools. A widget, a library, or your own code registered them on `document.modelContext`. You want your in-page chat to use the same tools, without a second copy of each tool.\n\nThe page tools API reads the tools from `document.modelContext` and gives them to the chat as client tools. When the model calls a tool, the chat runs the tool through WebMCP.\n\n> **Experimental:** WebMCP support is experimental. During SSR, in insecure contexts, or in unsupported browsers, the tool list stays empty.\n\n## 1. Accept client tools on the server\n\nThe server does not know the page tools. Let the client declare them with `mergeAgentTools`:\n\n```ts\n// api/chat.ts\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  mergeAgentTools,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-6-astra'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    tools: mergeAgentTools([], params.tools),\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\n> **Security:** `params.tools` comes from the browser. The model can call these tools, but the tools run in the browser, not on the server. Keep sensitive work behind your own server checks.\n\n## 2. Give the page tools to the chat\n\nUse the page tools API for your framework. Pass the result to the chat as `tools`.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n`usePageWebMCPTools` returns an array. The array updates when the page adds or removes a tool.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({ connection, tools: pageTools })\n\n  return (\n    <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n      Ask ({messages.length} messages)\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Vue\n\n`usePageWebMCPTools` returns a ref. Pass the ref to `useChat`.\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-vue'\n\nconst pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\nconst { sendMessage } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: pageTools,\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <button type=\"button\" @click=\"sendMessage('Open the help panel')\">\n    Ask\n  </button>\n</template>\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n`usePageWebMCPTools` returns an accessor. Read it in a `tools` getter.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    get tools() {\n      return pageTools()\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n      Ask\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Svelte\n\n`createPageWebMCPTools` returns an object with a reactive `tools` field. Read it in a `tools` getter.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import {\n    createChat,\n    createPageWebMCPTools,\n    fetchServerSentEvents,\n  } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n\n  const page = createPageWebMCPTools()\n  const chat = createChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    get tools() {\n      return page.tools\n    },\n  })\n</script>\n\n<button type=\"button\" onclick={() => chat.sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n  Ask\n</button>\n```\n\n# Preact\n\n`usePageWebMCPTools` returns an array. The array updates when the page adds or removes a tool.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-preact'\n\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({ connection, tools: pageTools })\n\n  return (\n    <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n      Ask\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Angular\n\n`injectPageWebMCPTools` returns a signal. Pass the signal to `injectChat`.\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  injectChat,\n  injectPageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-angular'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-chat',\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `<button type=\"button\" (click)=\"ask()\">Ask</button>`,\n})\nexport class Chat {\n  pageTools = injectPageWebMCPTools()\n  chat = injectChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    tools: this.pageTools,\n  })\n\n  ask() {\n    void this.chat.sendMessage('Open the help panel')\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Octane\n\n`usePageWebMCPTools` returns an array. The array updates when the page adds or removes a tool.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  useChat,\n  usePageWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-octane'\n\nconst connection = fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat')\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const pageTools = usePageWebMCPTools()\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({ connection, tools: pageTools })\n\n  return (\n    <button type=\"button\" onClick={() => sendMessage('Open the help panel')}>\n      Ask\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Remix\n\nPass the component `Handle` to `createPageWebMCPTools`. It calls `handle.update()` when the tools change. Read `page.tools` in a `tools` getter. The chat reads the getter each time a run starts.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createChat,\n  createPageWebMCPTools,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-remix'\nimport { clientEntry, createElement, on } from 'remix/ui'\n\nexport const Chat = clientEntry(import.meta.url, function Chat(handle) {\n  const page = createPageWebMCPTools(handle)\n  const chat = createChat(handle, {\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    get tools() {\n      return page.tools\n    },\n  })\n\n  return () =>\n    createElement(\n      'button',\n      {\n        type: 'button',\n        mix: on<HTMLButtonElement>('click', () => {\n          void chat.sendMessage('Open the help panel')\n        }),\n      },\n      'Ask',\n    )\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## 3. Skip tools with a filter\n\nPass `filter` to skip a tool. Return `false` and the chat does not get that tool. The filter gets the WebMCP tool, so you can read `name`, `origin`, and `annotations`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { usePageWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nexport function useReadOnlyPageTools() {\n  return usePageWebMCPTools({\n    filter: (tool) =>\n      tool.origin === location.origin &&\n      tool.annotations?.readOnlyHint === true,\n  })\n}\n```\n\nEvery framework API takes the same `filter` and `onError` options. `onError` gets a failed WebMCP read, for example a `NotAllowedError` from the `tools` permissions policy. The last good list stays in place.\n\nTool names must be unique after filtering, including tools from different frames. If names repeat, `getWebMCPTools()` rejects and subscriptions report the error through `onError`. Subscriptions keep the last good list. Give the tools unique names or use `filter` to select one of them.\n\nSome providers reject a tool name with a period, such as `help.open`. WebMCP allows periods. Skip those tools with `filter`.\n\n## Read page tools without a framework\n\nUse `getWebMCPTools` from `@tanstack/ai-client` to read the tools one time:\n\n```ts\nimport { ChatClient, fetchServerSentEvents, getWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: await getWebMCPTools(),\n})\n```\n\nTo keep the list current, use `subscribeWebMCPTools`. It calls your listener now and after each WebMCP `toolchange` event. Abort the signal to stop:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  ChatClient,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  subscribeWebMCPTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-client'\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n})\nconst subscription = new AbortController()\n\nsubscribeWebMCPTools((tools) => client.updateOptions({ tools }), {\n  signal: subscription.signal,\n  filter: (tool) => tool.origin === location.origin,\n})\n\nexport function stopPageTools() {\n  subscription.abort()\n}\n```\n\nEvery framework package also exports `getWebMCPTools` and `subscribeWebMCPTools`.\n\nYour chat can now call every WebMCP tool on the page that passes your filter. To expose your own client tools to WebMCP, see [WebMCP Tools](./webmcp).\n"}
